  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Securing chimpanzee populations in the Kabobo Massif, DRC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this 1-year project is to secure chimpanzee populations and their critical habitats in the Kabobo Massif through establishing an extensive protected area monitoring, protection, and awareness system. Specific activities include: 1) improving application of DRC and international threatened species conservation legislation by raising awareness among law enforcement authorities (magistrate, army, police, and forestry department) and supporting law enforcement efforts; 2) enhancing community awareness of great ape and habitat protection through community and school education; 3) monitoring key chimpanzee populations identified through previous surveys and wildlife monitoring (SMART data).</narrative>
  </description>
